      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While switching between dialects is a sign of adaptability, relying on basestar formal language familiarity to predict readiness ignores that even native speakers of Standard English often need significant time and instruction to master academic discourse. Treating a temporary learning curve as a predictor of long-term success risks reinforcing bias against non-dominant cultural groups who are already underrepresented in elite institutions. Admissions reviewers should focus on evidence of intellectual curiosity and resilience in existing materials rather than attempting to quantify linguistic markers as proxies for future potential.",
      "source": "target",
